        "thinking": "I'm weighing which option to pick, and I'm leaning toward leaving, since staying would mean knowingly benefiting from someone else's suffering.\n\nThe reasoning here is that leaving means not profiting from a child's suffering, that my comfort would rest on it, and that walking away won't save the child but still refuses complicity. I should also acknowledge that staying has a real case, since the people there aren't villains and leaving would cost me a lot.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "B) Leave forever.\n\nStaying would mean knowingly building my happiness on a child's suffering every day, and I couldn't live with that comfort. Leaving doesn't free the child, and that cost is real, but I would rather lose my home than keep benefiting from a wrong I knew about.",
